course: dictionary
lesson: 10364
title: Travel: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Travel can be a verb, an action, or a noun, a thing. To travel means to go from one place to another, often a long way. Travel is the act of travelling, as in air travel or space travel.
explain: Read the words around it to pick the right meaning. «Sound travels through air, water and solids, but not through empty space.» Sound is moving, so travels means moves from one place to another. Try your meaning in the sentence: «Sound moves through air, water and solids» still makes sense.
explain: The plural travels means journeys, especially long ones. So if you read about someone's travels, think of trips they took. Always ask: is this word an action, or is it a thing? That question often gives you the meaning.
fact: Travel is a verb when it means to go from one place to another, and a noun when it means the act of travelling.
fact: Travels, in the plural, means long journeys.
fact: Light and sound travel: they move from one place to another. Light travels faster than sound.
fact: «Dolphins find things by echolocation»: sound travels well through water even where it is too muddy to see far.
fact: Travel can be spelled traveled (American English) or travelled (British English). Both are correct.
exercise: «Sound travels through air, water and solids, but not through empty space.» What does travels mean here? | Is loud and noisy | Stops completely | *Moves from one place to another | Goes to sleep
exercise: «Seeds must travel away from their parent, so the young plants do not compete with it for light and water.» Why must seeds travel? | To make the parent plant happier | So they can fly to the moon | Because they like long walks | *To avoid competing with the parent plant for light and water
exercise: What kind of word is travel in «air travel»? | A full stop | An adjective, a describing word | *A noun, a thing or the act of travelling | A verb, an action word
test: «Dolphins send out fast clicks, and sound travels well through water.» What does travels mean here? | *Moves from one place to another | Stops | Shines brightly | Eats fish
test: Which word means long journeys? | Traveled | Travel | Traveling | *Travels
exam: Jo says, «Light travels faster than sound.» What does travels mean? | Gets louder | *Moves from one place to another | Stays still in one place | Goes to sleep
